      {
        "id": 230907,
        "name": "catDreaming",
        "username": "catDreaming",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-06-06T05:40:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hm... Well, there's nothing saying that a minor villain can't impact the Environment around them. I'd suggest building an environment for her encounters, reflecting the ambient power spikes that she generates. The twists from the environment could easily reflect that aspect of her powers, maybe something like:</p>\n<p>Forced Feedback: Boost one hero using the Max Die, then that hero loses health equal to the size of that bonus plus the Min die.</p>\n<p>Or, if there's a particular powered individual around, you could use the effects of her powers on that individual to guide environment twists.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ultimately though it's up to you.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
